!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/invalid/the-reference-constructor-applied-in-an-ordinary-schema-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §2.2.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §3.3.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    The structure namespace supplies the kernel's `ref_type` to a schema meta.tn governs, so the constructor
    can be applied directly where `ref<T>` cannot be named. A reference names an entry holding a value, and an
    ordinary schema declares only types, so a reference declared in one names nothing and is refused.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
